            <ArticleTitle>Postherpetic neuralgia: a workable treatment plan.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>34-6, 41-3, 47-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Management of established postherpetic neuralgia should proceed on several fronts simultaneously and may include pain-oriented treatments that are pharmacologic, neuroaugmentative, anesthetic, physiatric, psychological, and surgical. Many patients develop a pattern of abnormal illness behavior, manifesting loss of interest in work or avocations, social withdrawal, and disturbance of family roles. Improvement in these impairments must be a goal that is as important as amelioration of the pain itself.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
